 "SportPowerEndurance__B_Intermediate": {
  "1": [
   [
    "Finger Strength Test",
    "This 6-week program is designed for sport climbers with some experience with structured training that would like to build a foundation of power endurance to prepare for pumpy sport climbs. The template is designed to be split across three training days per week.  \n\nThe first training day can be completed at a boulder wall and should consist of the Warm Up, followed by either Boulder Intervals (weeks 1 & 2), Style Triad (Weeks 3 & 6), or Broken Quarters (weeks 4 & 5).  \n\nThe second training day will consist of the Route Warm Up Protocol followed by Route Pyramids (except for week 3).  \n\nThe third training day will consist of the Finger Strength Testing Session on week 1 and then on the remaining weeks will consist of 7:3s 50-60% repeaters.  The repeaters workouts can be done after max strength fingerboarding, but should not be done before strength training.  \n\nAdditional sessions can be added to this plan to maintain base endurance or strength & power."
   ],
   "Base"
  ],
